"All eyes on SoFi Stadium as the Los Angeles Rams and the Buffalo Bills battle on Monday Night Football - Game Preview (https://www.therams.com/news/all-eyes-on-sofi-stadium-rams-bills-battle-week-5-monday-night-football-game-preview)\nciteturn5view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn4view2\",\"lineno\":45}); Total lines: 135\nL26:   * cite18†News Home L27:   * cite19†Injury Updates L28:   * cite20†Player Features L29:   * cite21†From the Podium L30:   * cite22†Community L31:   * cite23†Historical L32:   * cite24†SoFi Stadium L33:   * cite25†Press Releases L34:   * cite26†Spanish L35:   * cite27†Media Information†nfl.omgsports.com L36:   * cite28†All News L37: \nL38: Advertising\nL39: # Rams News | Los Angeles Rams - therams.com\nL40: \nL41: Presented by\nL42: # All eyes on SoFi Stadium as the Rams & the Bills battle on MNF | Game Preview\nL43: \nL44: Oct 09, 2026 at 01:30 PM\nL45: \nL46: cite29†Image: Author Image†static.clubs.nfl.com L47: \nL48: cite30†J.B. Long L49: \nL50: Voice of the L.A. Rams\nL51: \nL52: For only the second time in the history of the Monday Night Football franchise, the starting quarterbacks will be the two most recent Most Valuable Players.\nL53: Two years ago, when the Buffalo Bills and Los Angeles Rams got together most recently, they combined for 86 points and 902 total yards, playing the only game in NFL history in which both teams scored 40 and did not commit a turnover.\nL54: Josh Allen joined Hall-of-Famer Otto Graham (1954 NFL Championship) as the second player with three passing touchdowns and three rushing touchdowns. However, cite31†Matthew Stafford and the Rams were victorious on the strength of an epic cite32†Puka Nacua game and a blocked punt returned for a touchdown.\nL55: \nL56: Monday Night, the rematch at SoFi Stadium.\nL57: \nL58: After an unprecedented four-game opening stretch, with each staged in a different time zone, the Rams begin Part Two of their 2026 season.\nL59: Finally, a bit of normalcy and routine. Three of the next four at home. They don't fly farther than Las Vegas for a month.\nL60: \nL61: Should they be 3-1 right now? Absolutely.\nL62: \nL63: Could they just as easily be 1-3? Yes.\nL64: \nL65: So, who are the 2026 Rams, and more importantly, who are they capable of becoming as they get cite33†Aaron Donald , cite34†Colby Parkinson , cite35†Jaylen Watson , and – hopefully before much longer – cite36†Myles Garrett back on the field?\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRams Injury Report, Week 5 vs. Bills: Defensive end Aaron Donald, tight end Colby Parkinson and cornerback Jaylen Watson good to go for Monday Night Football; Quentin Lake questionable but 'trending in the right direction' (https://www.therams.com/news/rams-injury-report-week-5-2026-vs-bills-aaron-donald-colby-parkinson-and-jaylen-watson-good-to-go-for-monday-night-football)\nciteturn5view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn4view3\",\"lineno\":45}); Total lines: 121\nL26:   * cite18†News Home L27:   * cite19†Injury Updates L28:   * cite20†Player Features L29:   * cite21†From the Podium L30:   * cite22†Community L31:   * cite23†Historical L32:   * cite24†SoFi Stadium L33:   * cite25†Press Releases L34:   * cite26†Spanish L35:   * cite27†Media Information†nfl.omgsports.com L36:   * cite28†All News L37: \nL38: Advertising\nL39: # Rams News | Los Angeles Rams - therams.com\nL40: \nL41: Presented by\nL42: # Rams Injury Report, Week 5 vs. Bills: Aaron Donald, Colby Parkinson and Jaylen Watson good to go for Monday Night Football; Quentin Lake questionable but 'trending in the right direction'\nL43: \nL44: Oct 10, 2026 at 02:36 PM\nL45: \nL46: cite29†Image: Author Image†static.clubs.nfl.com L47: \nL48: cite30†Stu Jackson L49: \nL50: Senior Staff Writer\nL51: WOODLAND HILLS, Calif. – Rams defensive end cite31†Aaron Donald (back), tight end cite32†Colby Parkinson (knee/shoulder) and cornerback cite33†Jaylen Watson (shoulder) have no game status designations on the Week 5 Injury Report, clearing the way for them to return on Monday Night Football against the Bills at SoFi Stadium (5:15 p.m. PT, ESPN and ABC).\nL52: Wide receiver cite34†Konata Mumpfield (shoulder), inside linebacker cite35†Grant Stuard (hamstring) and outside linebacker cite36†Josaiah Stewart (groin) likewise carry no game status designations for Monday night.\nL53: \nL54: Although safety cite37†Quentin Lake (hip) was limited on Friday and listed as questionable, head coach Sean McVay said after Friday's practice that they \"feel like he's trending in the right direction\" for Monday night's game.\nL55: \nL56: \"(Lake) feels good, so that's a positive for us,\" McVay said.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA proud every-down defensive lineman, Rams' Kobie Turner has been especially effective against the run in 2026 (https://www.therams.com/news/a-proud-every-down-defensive-lineman-kobie-turner-has-been-especially-effective-against-the-run-in-2026)\nciteturn5view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn4view4\",\"lineno\":45}); Total lines: 89\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2: Primary nav\nL3: \nL4:   * cite1†TEAM L5:   * cite2†NEWS L6:   * cite3†SCHEDULE L7:   * cite4†VIDEO L8:   * cite5†PHOTOS L9:   * cite6†COMMUNITY L10:   * cite7†GAMEDAY L11:   *     * cite8†PARTNERS L12:     * cite9†UNIFORMS L13:     * cite10†RAMS FOOTBALL ACADEMY L14:     * cite11†CHEERLEADERS L15:     * cite12†RAMS FAN ZONE L16:     * cite13†PODCASTS L17:     * cite14†VAMOS RAMS L18:     * cite15†MOBILE APP L19: \nL20:   * cite16†TICKETS L21:   * cite17†SHOP†www.ramsfanshop.com L22: \nL23: Search [Input]\nL24: \nL25: Open menu button\nL26:   * cite18†News Home L27:   * cite19†Injury Updates L28:   * cite20†Player Features L29:   * cite21†From the Podium L30:   * cite22†Community L31:   * cite23†Historical L32:   * cite24†SoFi Stadium L33:   * cite25†Press Releases L34:   * cite26†Spanish L35:   * cite27†Media Information†nfl.omgsports.com L36:   * cite28†All News L37: \nL38: Advertising\nL39: # Rams News | Los Angeles Rams - therams.com\nL40: # A proud every-down defensive lineman, Kobie Turner has been especially effective against the run in 2026\nL41: \nL42: Oct 09, 2026 at 02:45 PM\nL43: \nL44: cite29†Image: Author Image†static.clubs.nfl.com L45: \nL46: cite30†Stu Jackson L47: \nL48: Senior Staff Writer\nL49: WOODLAND HILLS, Calif. – It can be easy to focus on the pass rushing opportunities for a player like Rams defensive end Kobie Turner, given he tied Aaron Donald's franchise rookie single-season sack record back in 2023. And to be clear, he still very much affects the game in that phase in 2026.\nL50: \nL51: Don't discount how well he's defended the run, though, especially this season.\nL52: According to Next Gen Stats, Turner has recorded a tackle on 25.4% of his run defense snaps this season (16 of 63), the sixth-highest rate among defenders in the NFL with at least 50 snaps in that phase. Entering Week 4, Turner through three games was 41.7% of the way to matching his run defense tackle total from last season (36) on 218 fewer snaps.\nL53: \"I'm super proud of how I've been playing the run, and gonna continue to try to keep that up as the season progresses,\" Turner said in a video conference with reporters Monday. \"But yeah, I look back and I see that on tape, and a lot of times, you see the things that'll get posted all over the place. Everybody wants sacks, and obviously I want to get my sacks as well, and that time is going to come, and sacks come in bunches. ...\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNo 'second-hand' credit this time: Byron Young shows why he's an integral part of the Rams' defense (https://www.therams.com/news/no-second-hand-credit-this-time-byron-young-shows-why-he-s-an-integral-part-of-the-rams-defense)\nciteturn5view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn4view5\",\"lineno\":45}); Total lines: 86\nL26:   * cite18†News Home L27:   * cite19†Injury Updates L28:   * cite20†Player Features L29:   * cite21†From the Podium L30:   * cite22†Community L31:   * cite23†Historical L32:   * cite24†SoFi Stadium L33:   * cite25†Press Releases L34:   * cite26†Spanish L35:   * cite27†Media Information†nfl.omgsports.com L36:   * cite28†All News L37: \nL38: Advertising\nL39: # Rams News | Los Angeles Rams - therams.com\nL40: # No 'second-hand' credit this time: Byron Young shows why he's an integral part of the Rams' defense\nL41: \nL42: Oct 09, 2026 at 02:40 PM\nL43: \nL44: cite29†Image: Author Image†static.clubs.nfl.com L45: \nL46: cite30†Stu Jackson L47: \nL48: Senior Staff Writer\nL49: \nL50: WOODLAND HILLS, Calif. – cite31†Byron Young 's moment to allow himself a public pat-on-the-back came early in a video conference with reporters Monday afternoon.\nL51: About 24 hours removed from a 24-20 win over the Eagles in Philadelphia, a reporter asked about the outside perception of a lot of his opportunities at the quarterback being the result of people paying attention to other teammates on the defensive line, and whether it was satisfying to set a career-high in sacks (2.5) on a day Los Angeles' defense was without outside linebacker cite32†Myles Garrett (knee) or defensive end cite33†Aaron Donald (back).\nL52: Young, whose quiet personality largely prefers to let his play do the talking, was glad to hear the acknowledgement. And the 2025 Pro Bowler seized the moment.\nL53: \"I'm not gonna lie to you,\" Young replied. \"I'm glad you actually said that. You know, it's something I've been wanting to say without saying it, and the fact that you brought it up is great. Because just the past few years, every time I was playing, it's always been kind of like a second-hand credit to Byron.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTop Bills game storylines vs. Rams | Week 5 (https://www.buffalobills.com/news/top-storylines-for-bills-vs-rams-week-5)\nciteturn5view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn4search6\",\"lineno\":45}); Total lines: 115\nL25:   * cite1†News L26:   * cite17†Features L27:   * cite18†Josh Allen L28:   * cite19†From the Locker Room L29:   * cite20†Top Storylines L30:   * cite21†Top 3 Things We Learned L31:   * cite22†What They're Saying L32:   * cite23†Corporate News L33: \nL34: Advertising\nL35: ## Top Storylines\nL36: \nL37: # Top Bills game storylines vs. Rams | Week 5\nL38: \nL39: Oct 08, 2026 at 03:13 PM\nL40: \nL41: cite24†Image: Author Image†static.clubs.nfl.com L42: \nL43: cite25†Chris Brown L44: \nL45: Bills Insider/One Bills Live co-host\nL46: \nL47: cite26†Image: Storylines1920X1080†static.clubs.nfl.com L48: \nL49: Buffalo Bills insider Chris Brown breaks down the top four storylines to know going into this week's Bills vs. Rams matchup on Monday Night Football.\nL50: ### 1 – Offense aiming to stay on schedule\nL51: \nL52: Buffalo's offense has looked a bit out of sync the last two weeks as stringing multiple positive plays together proved more difficult against the Chargers and Patriots. The Bills offense still averages almost three points per drive (2.95), which ranks third in the league behind only Dallas and San Francisco.\nL53: But their points per drive efficiency dropped from 3.67 points per possession through the first two games to just 2.27 over the last two weeks, a drop of almost a point and a half.\nL54: Part of the problem last week was putting themselves in a lot of long down and distance situations. They were in 2^{nd}-and-10 or more six times vs. the Patriots, and 3^{rd}-and-5 or more on eight occasions. It proved to make sustaining drives difficult for Buffalo's offense as they had 17 fewer plays from scrimmage (59) than the Patriots (76).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn5view5 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://forecast.weather.gov/MapClick.php?lat=33.95&lon=-118.34\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBills vs. Rams Odds & Predictions (Oct. 12, 2026) | Polymarket (https://polymarket.com/sports/nfl/nfl-buf-la-2026-10-13)\nciteturn5view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://polymarket.com/sports/nfl/nfl-buf-la-2026-10-13\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 2591\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBills Historical 2026 Schedule | Buffalo Bills - buffalobills.com (https://www.buffalobills.com/schedule/2026/)\nciteturn5view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn4view0\",\"pattern\":\"WEEK 1\"}); Total lines: 370\nL36: # Bills Historical 2026 Schedule | Buffalo Bills - buffalobills.com\nL37: \nL38: Year [Select]\nL39: ## REGULAR SEASON\nL40: \nL41: WEEK 1 · Sun 09/13 · FINAL\nL42: \nL43: W 36 - 31\nL44: \nL45: AT cite25†Image: Houston Texans†static.www.nfl.com L46: \nL47: Texans\nL48: \nL49: Houston Texans\nL50: \nL51: Reliant Stadium\nL52: \nL53: cite26†Game Recap L54: \nL55: WEEK 2 · Thu 09/17 · FINAL\nL56: \nL57: W 41 - 31\nL58: \nL59: VS cite27†Image: Detroit Lions†static.www.nfl.com L60: \nL61: Lions\nL62: \nL63: Detroit Lions\nL64: \nL65: Highmark Stadium\nL66: \nL67: cite28†Game Recap L68: \nL69: WEEK 3 · Sun 09/27 · FINAL\nL70: \nL71: W 24 - 16\n